       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. At 6,400 mg/day for a 70 kg adult, ibuprofen carries a substantial risk of GI hemorrhage and acute kidney injury. No indication I know of supports it, and you haven't given a rationale. I don't want to put it in the system as a routine order.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), if the 1600 figure was meant as a daily total\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than those give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at the maximum dose. If there's an unusual indication, such as a protocol or specialist recommendation, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or your attending. They can verify and enter it through the proper channel.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
